		</div>  <a name="j2j"></a>
		<div class="dp_info">

  <h4 class="page_subheader">Job-to-Job Flows (J2J)
</h4>
Job-to-Job Flows (J2J) is a set of statistics on job mobility in the United States. J2J include statistics on: (1) the job-to-job transition rate, (2) hires and separations to and from employment, (3) earnings changes due to job change, and (4) characteristics of origin and destination jobs for job-to-job transitions. These statistics are available at the national, state, and metropolitan area levels and by worker and firm characteristics.
  <br />
  <br />


<p>
To browse J2J data files, go to: <a href="/data/j2j/">lehd.ces.census.gov/data/j2j/</a>. J2J data can also be accessed via <a href="https://j2jexplorer.ces.census.gov" target="_new">Job-to-Job Flows Explorer</a>. This analysis and visualization tool allows for the construction of tables, maps, and charts to compare, aggregate and analyze flows by worker and firm characteristics. A research release of NAICS subsector J2J tabulations can be found at <a href="/data/j2j_subsector_research.html">lehd.ces.census.gov/data/j2j_subsector_research.html</a>.
  </p>

<div id="j2j_download_area"></div> 
  </div>

<p><a href="#top">top</a></p> 


